390 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (In the Kingdom of Marilag, the sea has long provided wealth and life to its people. But when failed harvests, disappearing merchant ships, and a devastating storm leave the kingdom vulnerable, a powerful neighboring sultanate offers aid in exchange for one thing: the marriage of Princess Hiraya to its heir, Ladja Makusug.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (To Hiraya, the offer seems too generous to be without consequence. As she uncovers troubling signs behind Marilag's growing misfortunes, she begins to question whether the promised alliance is truly an act of friendship or a carefully planned attempt to claim her kingdom.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Caught between her duty to her people and the demands of powerful rulers, Hiraya must discover what it truly means to lead. For when the fate of Marilag hangs in the balance, its future may depend not on the strength of its crown, but on the courage of those who call it home.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 180 0 R
/T (A crown may be inherited, and a kingdom may be conquered, but neither makes a true ruler. For a throne means little when its bearer has forgotten the very people it was meant to serve.)
/E (A crown may be inherited, and a kingdom may be conquered, but neither makes a true ruler. For a throne means little when its bearer has forgotten the very people it was meant to serve.)
/Pg 42 0 R
/K [6]
>>
