/Title (Makusug brought to Hiraya the proposal of Sultan Jalal. Akbar was to send grains, soldiers and ships in order for Marilag to recover from the flooding. However, the marriage proposal had to be preserved. The offer was even more generous after the flood, but it may also contain dangers.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1084 0 R
/Next 1088 0 R
>>
endobj
1087 0 obj
<<
/Title (Makusug did not know whether his father had ordered the attacks on the merchant ships. But his uncertainty only made Hiraya more worried. If Akbar had created the very conditions that made Marilag desperate for protection, then their offer was not an act of friendship. It was a carefully prepared opportunity.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1089 0 R
/Next 1085 0 R
>>
endobj
1088 0 obj
<<
/Title (Later, an old sailor showed her a piece of blue fabric with the symbol of Akbar. The sailor referred to the remaining sailors that had survived and told about armed men dressed in similar outfits.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1086 0 R
/Next 1090 0 R
>>
endobj
1089 0 obj
<<
/Title (Its location gave it access to important maritime routes, fertile lands, and a harbor that could strengthen Akbar's control over trade. The marriage would not simply unite two royal families. It would place Marilag's future closer to the hands of Akbar.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1091 0 R
/Next 1087 0 R
>>
endobj
1090 0 obj
<<
/Title (When Hiraya encountered Makusug again, she found him more difficult to understand than she expected. He did not behave like an enemy. He spoke respectfully to the people of Marilag and showed concern for the families affected by the storm.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1088 0 R
/Next 1091 0 R
>>
endobj
1091 0 obj
<<
/Title (Yet he knew less about his father's plans than Hiraya expected. Makusug admitted that Sultan Jalal believed Marilag was too valuable to remain weak.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1090 0 R
/Next 1089 0 R
>>
endobj
